{"name":"Crocodile Style","hex":"#767437","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crocodile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the predatory amphibious reptiles of the family Crocodylidae;  a crocodilian, any species of the order Crocodilia, which also includes the alligators, caimans and gavials.","A long line or procession of people (especially children) walking together."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak another language than Esperanto at an Esperanto-language gathering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodile"},{"term":"style","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Senses relating to a thin, pointed object.\n A sharp stick used for writing on clay tablets or other surfaces; a stylus;  an instrument used to write with ink; a pen.\n\nA tool with a sharp point used in engraving; a burin, a graver, a stylet, a stylus.\n\nThe gnomon or pin of a sundial, the shadow of which indicates the hour.\n\n The stalk that connects the stigma(s) to the ovary in a pistil of a flower.","A sharp stick used for writing on clay tablets or other surfaces; a stylus;  an instrument used to write with ink; a pen."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To design, fashion, make, or arrange in a certain way or form (style).","To call or give a name or title to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/style"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocodile","blocks":[{"text":"A crocodile or true crocodile is a large, semiaquatic reptile that lives throughout the tropics in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Australia. The term \"crocodile\" is sometimes used more loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes the alligators and caimans, the gharial and false gharial as well as other extinct taxa. This article uses \"crocodile\" or \"true crocodile\" to refer only to the species taxonomically included in the Crocodylidae family, extant or extinct."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons